{"name":"Nordland Blue","hex":"#7e95ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nordland","blocks":[{"text":"Nordland is one of the three northernmost counties in Norway in the Northern Norway region, bordering Troms in the north, Trøndelag in the south, Norrbotten County in Sweden to the east, Västerbotten County to the south-east, and the Atlantic Ocean to the west. The county was formerly known as Nordlandene amt. The county administration is in the town of Bodø. The remote Arctic island of Jan Mayen has been administered from Nordland since 1995. In the southern part of the county is Vega, listed on the UNESCO World Heritage Site list."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Bj%C3%B8rkneset_fra_Tekoppstetten._Lofoten_in_North_Norway.jpg/330px-Bj%C3%B8rkneset_fra_Tekoppstetten._Lofoten_in_North_Norway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nordland","wikidata":"Q50630"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ballstad_Lofoten.JPG/500px-Ballstad_Lofoten.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ballstad_Lofoten.JPG/1280px-Ballstad_Lofoten.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Ballstad_Lofoten.JPG/500px-Ballstad_Lofoten.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ballstad in Lofoten","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABallstad_Lofoten.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Trollfjord_from_the_opposite_coast_of_Raftsundet_3.JPG/500px-Trollfjord_from_the_opposite_coast_of_Raftsundet_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Trollfjord_from_the_opposite_coast_of_Raftsundet_3.JPG/1280px-Trollfjord_from_the_opposite_coast_of_Raftsundet_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Trollfjord_from_the_opposite_coast_of_Raftsundet_3.JPG/500px-Trollfjord_from_the_opposite_coast_of_Raftsundet_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Autumn near Trollfjord in Hadsel Municipality. Nordland is home to innumerable fjords and fjord branches.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrollfjord_from_the_opposite_coast_of